================================================================================
2026-07-25 — ALL THREE HighAsCG-MODULE ISSUES ROOT-CAUSED + FIXED IN v1.0.4
(companion-module-dev commit b209e09; packaged highpass-highascg-1.0.4.tgz)
================================================================================
Context: the box runs module 1.0.3 since this morning's install (~11:04) — that
install is what surfaced the WoL section (added in 1.0.3, WO-216).

1. WoL options + can't save config → WoL REMOVED ENTIRELY (owner decision).
   The regex-validated WoL fields also blocked saving while EMPTY — Companion 5
   validates `regex` even on optional empty textinputs, so the form was
   permanently invalid out of the box.
2. "layered preset definitions contain invalid elements: Preview chN ·
   Bottom-right" → the BR screen badge used x:-20; Companion 5's element schema
   bounds x/y/w/h to 0..100 and rejects the whole preset. Re-expressed in-range
   (x:0 w:80 halign right). Only BR quads used a negative x — matches the log.
3. look_take "Value is not in the list of choices" (button 1/0/1) → verified in
   Companion's DB: the stored buttons have NO `target` option (saved before the
   Bus dropdown existed); Companion 5 hard-fails strict dropdowns on missing
   values BEFORE the callback. target is now allowCustom; callback defaults to
   program. (Alternative: delete + re-add the button from the preset.)

NOT ours: pixelhue discovery timeouts to 192.168.50.34:19998 — third-party
module; the device is unreachable on the network (powered off / wrong IP).

TO DEPLOY 1.0.4 (drops the desk ~30s):
  sudo systemctl stop companion \
    && ~/highascg/tools/eggs/companion/install-companion-module.sh \
    && sudo systemctl start companion
